<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Primera Junta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1810</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Primera Junta was the first autonomous government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a>, formed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> on 25 May 1810 after the May Revolution deposed the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> Baltasar Hidalgo de Cisneros. Presided over by Cornelio Saavedra, with Mariano Moreno and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-belgrano">Manuel Belgrano</a> among its members, it sent armies to the interior, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-peru">Upper Peru</a>. It was enlarged into the Junta Grande in December 1810.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/primera-junta.jpg" alt="Primera Junta" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francisco Fortuny · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Primera_junta_por_Francisco_Fortuny.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
